@title Earthworm Jim 2 (USA)
@file Earthworm Jim 2 (U).gba
@game AJ4E
@save none
@chip none (password game: no save library string, title menu offers New Game / Options / Password; the pause screen shows the level password)
@frozen dingbat-bios,mgba,nba

# The game has no battery save: progress is carried by passwords (the pause
# screen prints the current one). This plays the logos, the title menu, the
# Options screen, New Game and the first stretch of the first level (walk
# right, two shots, the waterfall, a gun pickup on the far ledge), with the
# pause screen's password in between. No [load].
# Notes (2026-10-15): the second reference holds the Majesco logo longer
# (still on it at f1200, when dingbat and mgba show "Conversion by", and on
# "Conversion by" at f1500, when they show Playmates / Shiny), yet reaches
# the title menu with them; its menu letters bounce at another phase
# (title_menu MAJOR, it alone), and by options the three meet (SLIP -1). From level_start mgba's level differs: a crow attacks
# earlier, Jim takes damage (90%, then 80%) and the pause password ends
# CXJB86 where dingbat and the second reference show CXJB8W. dingbat and
# the second reference agree on the level (level_start IDENTICAL,
# waterfall SLIP +0); the pause menu's bouncing letters differ in phase.

[new]
wait 600
wait 300
wait 600
wait 400
checkpoint title_menu window=30
press DOWN after=30
press A after=90
checkpoint options window=30
press B after=60
wait 90
press UP after=30
press UP after=30
press UP hold=8 after=30
press A after=300
wait 200
checkpoint level_start window=30
hold RIGHT
wait 120
release
press B after=40
hold RIGHT
wait 90
release
wait 60
checkpoint waterfall window=30
hold RIGHT
wait 150
release
wait 30
press START after=60
checkpoint pause_password window=30
press A after=60
hold RIGHT
wait 60
press B hold=10
wait 60
press B hold=10
wait 60
release
wait 30
checkpoint gun_pickup window=30
